<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Open&nbsp;for&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>My biggest concerns with this SCP are twofold:</p>
<p>1. The entire proposal is extremely focussed on what the SCP is to the point where you don't even mention the PoV characters at all (i.e., the Foundation).</p>
<p>2. There's no real growth or change over it.</p>
<p>The first is my general sign that a tale from the perspective of the SCP might be more interesting than a SCP article, in that, if you think the SCPs internal life and what happens to them is the most interesting aspect of the story, it's generally best to tell the story from that perspective so you don't have to rely on the SCP telling the Foundation what's up. It's also generally a good idea if you don't have a strong thing for the Foundation to be trying to do because it means you don't have to worry about questions like 'why are the Foundation doing this'.</p>
<p>The second is a bigger concern: at the end of the day, you're trying to tell a story, and they're fundamentally characterised by things happening and like, characters changing or the situation they're in changing or w/e, and at the moment, it just feels&#8230;like you have a very generic overview of how this works without a clear like, end goal in mind? E.g., the SCP doesn't grow emotionally, they don't strive to overcome anything, there's not even any specific events mentioned; and I just really want to see something more concrete using this, y'know?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

