			<div class="content" id="post-content-4823673">
									

<p>1) Obligatory: New to this so expect some weird questions. So&#8230;is it possible to write a tale about an SCP without having an SCP article about said SCP? For some reason it felt like it was necessary to write the article about the SCP before the story about the SCP in order to get the number. The story is essentially written, I just wasn't sure if, for the purposes of this site, it was necessary to have the SCP first and then the story.</p>
<p>I'm just not sure about the order here. It just felt weird having the story first without having a number, if that makes any sense.</p>
<p>2) I was trying to keep it to the 400-word limit. This is a weird character to write about because The Foundation obviously wants to stop the character because the character's very existence requires the death of others, even as the character is on a road of self-discovery. The irony here is that the character is prevented from finding out the biggest part of who he is by the nature of his being.</p>
<p>[Yes, I was working on having the character basically working like a weekly show but from the bad guy's perspective, but where the bad guy didn't realize he was the bad guy.]</p>

